    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests that {@link LocalDate#until(java.time.chrono.ChronoLocalDate)} returns a zero period when the target {@link JulianDate} denotes the very same point on the time-line as the ISO date. <p> Each sample pairs a {@code JulianDate} with the ISO {@code LocalDate} that represents the identical day (for example, {@code 0001-01-01 (Julian)} is {@code 0000-12-30 (ISO)}). Because the two values are the same day, the period between them must be {@link Period#ZERO}."
